<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Samick defaults on notes-Yonha.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Samick defaults on notes-Yonha.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's leading piano manufacturer Samick Musical Instruments Co Ltd defaulted on Wednesday on payments of 2.7 billion won worth of promissory notes, the domestic Yonhap news agency reported.</p>
<p>Yonhap said Samick's primary bank the Korea Exchange Bank refused to pay the notes in lieu of the piano maker, which recently suffered from a fund squeeze due to a slump in sales.</p>
<p>Samick's borrowings from financial institutions totalled 283 billion won, while its assets totalled 372.6 billion won, Yonhap said.</p>
</text>
